# The alignment canary, re-exposed rather than recomputed.
#
# `Ring::on_distinct_lines` delegates to `CursorPair::on_distinct_lines`, which
# is unconditionally true by the reasoning in `ring_cursor.accepted`. A wrapper
# around a constant is a constant. Re-exposed here so a caller holding a `Ring`
# can make the check without reaching for the pair.
#
# See accepted/readme.md, "The alignment canaries".

ring_spsc/src/lib.rs:451:5: replace Ring<S>::on_distinct_lines -> bool with true

# The consumer's reload test, off by one in the harmless direction.
#
# `Consumer::observe_produced` reloads the producer cursor only when the
# records the consumer already knows of are fewer than the drain asks for.
# Turning `<` into `<=` also reloads when they are exactly enough. The drain
# then hands out the same records from a fresher observation; nothing a test
# can see differs, only one atomic load per lap boundary. Equivalent mutant.
# See docs/decisions/002_the_consumer_caches_the_producer_cursor.md.

ring_spsc/src/lib.rs:1104:59: replace < with <= in Consumer<'_, S>::observe_produced
